    <briefdescription>
<para>Internal helper that computes and paints tick marks and labels for a single <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1Axis" kindref="compound">Axis</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tick computation and painting are split: <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1AxisTickPainter_1ab562bfd5e90de190ede26dee32247ae7" kindref="member">computeTicks()</ref></computeroutput> formats labels and must run on the formatter&apos;s (GUI) thread, while <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1AxisTickPainter_1ac1c0a474b369ec774d8e969ce16b91a0" kindref="member">paintTicks()</ref></computeroutput> only draws precomputed ticks and is safe to call from <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1Axis_1a3613ed1b3cae19f09cc42571153a751c" kindref="member">Axis::paint()</ref></computeroutput> on the render thread. Also provides <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1AxisTickPainter_1abcb7eeba5fcb783759bbe4c62413bf40" kindref="member">computeNiceStep()</ref></computeroutput>, which is shared with <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1GridNode" kindref="compound">GridNode</ref></computeroutput> to keep grid lines aligned with tick positions. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
